%% Sequence 04d — Stage and dispatch AI dispute evaluation
%% Evidence status: Partial. Suar persistence, fencing, audit, and the trigger contract are implemented; the external advisory service is configurable.
%% Parent use case: UC 03b “Inspect AI advisory”, extending governed dispute resolution.
%% Design-class trace: cls_03k1--03k3 resolve the AI-evaluation API boundary into inbound construction, governed source context, and fenced gateway responsibilities.
%% Scenario: a system administrator requests one advisory evaluation for a review-dispute case file.
%% Scope: the primary immediate-dispatch interaction. Deferred reconciliation reuses the same durable evaluation but is a separate recovery operation; the signed callback is the next focused interaction in seq_04e.

sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor A as System administrator
    participant B as «boundary» AI evaluation API
    participant G as «outbound» Evaluation gateway
    participant DB as «store» PostgreSQL
    participant X as «external» Clawagent API

    A->>B: POST advisory evaluation
    B->>DB: Read role, dispute, and case-file snapshot
    DB-->>B: Eligible advisory context
    B->>B: Validate AI eligibility and dossier
    B->>G: Stage payload and callback identifiers
    G->>DB: Commit evaluation, trigger payload, and audit
    G-->>B: Durable staged evaluation
    B->>G: Dispatch staged evaluation
    G->>DB: Claim fenced dispatch attempt
    G->>X: Signed advisory request
    X-->>G: Accepted or classified failure
    G->>DB: Record acceptance and enter ai_reviewing
    G-->>B: Dispatch state
    B-->>A: 201 advisory evaluation accepted
